        paragraphs: [
          `For centuries, society dictated what women's purpose should be: raising children, supporting a partner, contributing to the home. As women increasingly reject these narrow definitions, they find that purpose is not something imposed but something deeply personal. For single women, this realisation can be liberating. Without the societal expectations tied to marriage or motherhood, they have the unusual opportunity to craft lives entirely their own. The question is not what should I be doing, but what brings me joy. Finding new purpose is not about reinventing yourself into someone completely new. It is about reconnecting with the parts of you that may have been overlooked or undervalued.`,
        ],
